      "title": "4: Simulation Is Not Instantiation",
      "gist": "Simulating a process, like digestion or a rainstorm, does not create the real thing, so simulating a brain computationally would only create consciousness if computation itself were sufficient for it, an assumption left unexamined even in ideas like the simulation hypothesis.",
      "sourceHeading": "4: Simulation Is Not Instantiation"
