      "range": [
        "spya-e7fdmb",
        "spya-d89xf7"
      ],
      "title": "What (Not) To Do?",
      "gist": "Given deep uncertainty about machine consciousness, we should avoid deliberately creating it while still taking seriously the separate ethical dangers posed by AI that merely seems conscious.",
      "question": "Conscious AI's uncertainty — what should we actually do given we cannot be sure? (a recommendation)",
      "sourceHeading": "What (Not) To Do?"
    },
    "n0134": {
      "id": "n0134",
      "depth": 2,
      "parent": "n0133",
      "children": [
        "n0135",
        "n0136",
        "n0137",
        "n0138"
      ],
      "range": [
        "spya-e7fdmb",
        "spya-zajp75"
      ],
      "title": "Why the fact matters",
      "gist": "Whether AI is really conscious determines its moral status, so despite remaining uncertainty and minority disagreement about the biological naturalist view, we should not pretend the question is settled."
    },
